# Versions of cicaid-devtools (public leonarduk/cicaid) and
# cicaid-devtools-pro (private leonarduk/cicaid-pro) that the AI PR review
# workflow installs. The two install side by side: cicaid_devtools is a
# namespace package, so the pro package's review modules merge into it.
#
# This lives outside .github/workflows/ deliberately: GitHub hard-blocks a
# workflow's default GITHUB_TOKEN from pushing any change under that
# directory, whatever permissions the job is granted, so a pin written
# inline in a workflow file can only ever be bumped by a PAT carrying the
# `workflow` scope. Keeping it here lets update-dependencies.yml bump it
# unattended (leonarduk/cicaid-pro#527, #6597).
#
# requirements-automation.txt pins the same versions; both files are
# rewritten together by scripts/update_dependency_pins.py, which fails if
# they ever disagree.
#
# Only KEY=<tag> lines are honoured; the install step rejects anything else.
CICAID_REF=v0.5.10
CICAID_PRO_REF=v0.19.0
